WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:02.961
(Teacher vocalizing)

00:00:02.961 --> 00:00:04.630
We have to write an essay?

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:06.298
(Teacher vocalizing)

00:00:06.298 --> 00:00:08.300
Five hundred words
about who we are?

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.093
I have no idea who I am.

00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:11.929
Good grief.

00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:14.014
You worry too much,
Charlie Brown.

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:17.809
WOMAN: Long before there was
a boy named Charlie Brown,

00:00:17.809 --> 00:00:20.854
there was a man named
Charles Schulz.

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:23.232
Even as a kid,
I was cognizant of the fact

00:00:23.232 --> 00:00:25.525
that there is a man
somewhere in America

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:27.861
who sits at a large,
slanted desk,

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.529
and he draws "Peanuts."

00:00:31.573 --> 00:00:33.575
"Peanuts" is just
its own planet.

00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:35.953
I related to Charlie Brown
so much.

00:00:35.953 --> 00:00:38.747
I think Charlie Brown is just
a little bit of what all
of us have

00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:40.958
inside of us.

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.586
My favorite character is Linus.

00:00:44.586 --> 00:00:46.463
I used to carry around
a blue blanket.

00:00:46.463 --> 00:00:49.258
Everybody knows what Lucy
with the football means.

00:00:49.258 --> 00:00:50.717
Ugh!

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:53.345
I love Snoopy.
He is so cute.

00:00:53.345 --> 00:00:54.471
(screaming)

00:00:58.141 --> 00:01:00.477
SCHULZ:
Been dreaming about this thing
since I was about six years old.

00:01:00.477 --> 00:01:03.105
PAIGE BRADDOCK:
He was the little kid
that no one really talked to.

00:01:03.105 --> 00:01:05.148
(typing)

00:01:05.148 --> 00:01:08.819
He was one person telling
a personal story every day.

00:01:11.697 --> 00:01:15.492
Like all best creators,
there's a lot of himself
in the work.

00:01:15.492 --> 00:01:18.954
I remember I called him
"my sweet Babboo."

00:01:18.954 --> 00:01:20.706
Pretty soon it was
in the comic strip.

00:01:20.706 --> 00:01:22.207
And he-- he was
those characters.

00:01:22.207 --> 00:01:23.959
I have to figure out
the meaning of my life.

00:01:23.959 --> 00:01:27.296
The meaning of life is
to give and receive love.

00:01:27.296 --> 00:01:29.798
I feel like he always was
searching for the truth

00:01:29.798 --> 00:01:31.466
and wanted
the world to be equal.

00:01:31.466 --> 00:01:34.052
You saw the girls in sports,
which as a girl,

00:01:34.052 --> 00:01:35.345
I'm like,
"Oh, that's great."

00:01:35.345 --> 00:01:37.431
Here I am reading
this comic strip,

00:01:37.431 --> 00:01:39.474
and all of a sudden,
there's a kid in there
that looks like me.

00:01:39.474 --> 00:01:43.145
In was 1968,
papers threatened
to drop the strip--

00:01:43.145 --> 00:01:45.522
And he was like,
"Fine, drop it."

00:01:45.522 --> 00:01:49.443
The conversations
those young children have 
resonates to our soul.

00:01:49.443 --> 00:01:52.154
As successful as he was,

00:01:52.154 --> 00:01:56.116
I don't know that he got
the full depth of the love

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:59.953
and devotion people had
to him and those characters.

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.371
SCHULZ:
Keep on trying.

00:02:01.371 --> 00:02:02.831
Charlie Brown never gives up.

00:02:02.831 --> 00:02:04.583
And if anybody should give up,
he should.

00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:05.917
(chuckles) 

00:02:07.878 --> 00:02:09.755
♪♪ (theme plays)

